        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current procedures and confirm scope of the integrated support programme.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the Integrated Early Support Programme. To get started on T1, could everyone briefly share their current process for identifying and referring at-risk children? This will be crucial for building the mapping document, A1.",
            "mentions": [
              350111,
              361403,
              427511,
              511446
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good morning. In my classroom, it's mainly based on observation and professional judgement. If we have a concern, we have an informal chat with the school lead, but there isn't a standardised form we use before that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Same for me! I keep a little notebook where I write down any worries. We also have the daily handover sheet between staff, we could just add a section to that!",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing. From the social services side, we have a formal intake process, but the information we receive from schools can be very inconsistent. That's the gap T1 is meant to address. Using informal notebooks or handover sheets raises data protection questions we'll need to solve with the new protocol.",
            "mentions": [
              350111
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Exactly, @361403. That's a key risk. The purpose of A1 is to get all these different methods documented so we can design a single, safe process. I've already started a draft for A1 based on the school handbook and can share it for everyone to add their parts.",
            "mentions": [
              361403
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 427511,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Sorry for the delay. What is A1?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "@427511, A1 is the 'Current Procedures Mapping Document'. It's the first step for task T1. @499701 has started a draft for us.",
            "mentions": [
              427511,
              499701
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "No problem @427511. I can take the lead on compiling everyone's input into the A1 document. Let's make that official, I'll take ownership.",
            "mentions": [
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Next, let's decide on the pilot scope, which is part of T9. The initial proposal is for two classes. Given the tight timeline, does that feel manageable to everyone?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Two classes sounds about right. Any more and we might struggle to give the pilot the focus it needs.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Yes two is perfect! We can do it!",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "raised_hands",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "I agree, two classes is a good starting point. We should also be clear on the 'types of cases' we'll include. I suggest we focus on wellbeing and engagement concerns initially, rather than complex special educational needs.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 427511,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "what about children who are absent a lot?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Good point @427511. Let's include attendance concerns as a key flag. So, to confirm the decision: the pilot will run in two classes, focusing on cases related to wellbeing, engagement, and attendance. I'll update the pilot plan, A7, to reflect this.",
            "mentions": [
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Sounds good. I'll add my notes on the current social work referral process to the draft A1 by the end of the day.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "I'll do the same for my classroom procedures.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
