      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define classroom support routines and align them with school procedures and workload.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's move on to T6. I've drafted a list of potential Classroom Support Routines for the A4 guideline. The goal is to agree on 5-8 practical strategies that don't add significant workload. Are these realistic for our classrooms?",
            "mentions": [
              511446,
              350111,
              361403,
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Thanks for drafting this, @499701. The 'visual timetable' and 'calm-down corner' are great ideas. The 'daily check-in circle' might be hard to fit in every single day. Could we aim for 3 times a week?",
            "mentions": [
              499701
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "I love the calm-down corner idea! We could put glitter jars and squishy toys in it! What about a buddy system with older kids?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "sparkles",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "These are very practical strategies. The 'emotional vocabulary cards' will be great for supporting social-emotional needs. A buddy system is a nice idea, @350111, but it might be best to keep this pilot focused on routines managed within the classroom to avoid complexity.",
            "mentions": [
              350111
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Good feedback all. @511446, changing the check-in to 3x/week is a smart adjustment. @361403, I agree on keeping it classroom-focused. So, how about this as our final list of 6 strategies? 1. Visual Timetable, 2. Calm-down Corner, 3. Emotional Vocabulary Cards, 4. 3x Weekly Check-in Circle, 5. Task Chunking, 6. Positive Reinforcement Chart.",
            "mentions": [
              511446,
              361403
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 427511,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "who pays for the things for the calm-down corner?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "We have a small budget for classroom materials, @427511. We can make most of it with things we already have.",
            "mentions": [
              427511
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "That list of 6 looks solid. It's a great, manageable set for the pilot.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Yes! Looks good!",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Great. Let's confirm that as our selected set of classroom support strategies. Now, how should we document and store this for staff access? Should A4 be a printed poster, a digital doc, or something else?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5",
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "A digital document is essential for updates, but a one-page printout in each classroom would be a very helpful quick reminder.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "I agree, both would be ideal. The digital version is the source of truth, and the printout is a practical job aid.",
            "mentions": [],
