      {
        "thread_id": "TH5",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in monitoring indicators, reporting template, and pilot start date.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M74",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi everyone, we're nearly there. For T8 and T12, I've created the Monitoring and Reporting Template (A6) and proposed 3 indicators to evaluate the pilot's impact: 1. Reduction in classroom incidents, 2. Improvement in attendance, 3. Teacher rating of child wellbeing (1-5 scale). What are your thoughts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8",
              "T12",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M75",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M74",
            "text": "Thanks @361403. The template A6 is clean and simple. For the wellbeing rating, we should provide a simple rubric with descriptions for what a 1, 3, and 5 mean to ensure we're all scoring consistently. I can draft something for that.",
            "mentions": [
              361403
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M76",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M74",
            "text": "The template looks easy to fill out, which is great. A rubric for the wellbeing score would be very helpful, I agree with @499701. How often would we need to complete this?",
            "mentions": [
              499701
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M77",
            "speaker_id": 361403,
            "reply_to": "M76",
            "text": "Good question. I was thinking a baseline at the start of the pilot, and then a quick update every two weeks. Does that sound manageable?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M78",
            "speaker_id": 511446,
            "reply_to": "M77",
            "text": "Every two weeks feels right. Frequent enough to be useful but not a daily burden.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M79",
            "speaker_id": 350111,
            "reply_to": "M77",
            "text": "So we fill this in, and we also do the observation checklist? Are they two different forms?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M80",
            "speaker_id": 499701,
            "reply_to": "M79",
            "text": "Yes, @350111. The observation checklist (A3) is our quick, weekly tool for noting specific behaviours. This new template (A6) is for the fortnightly summary to track overall progress against the pilot's goals. The checklist notes will help you fill in the summary.",
            "mentions": [
              350111
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
